CM_ "Peugeot 308 II T9 2018 AEE2010.full. This file contains only signals decoded and validated or manually confirmed on the local vehicle captures. It is a receive-only description and does not authorize CAN transmission.";
CM_ "Signal layouts are derived in part from commaai/opendbc psa_aee2010_r3.dbc revision a0febba355168a5cb6168b535144c8c41a5ce323, Copyright (c) 2020 Comma.ai, Inc., MIT License. Vehicle-specific validation was performed by the local OBD project.";
CM_ "PSA four-bit CHECKSUM fields use checksum=(CHK_INI-sum(payload nibbles with checksum cleared))&0xF. Equivalently, the sum of all transmitted nibbles modulo 16 equals CHK_INI. The protected frames and initial values in this file were exhaustively checked over 72 local learn sessions (2.9 GB).";
CM_ "Vehicle BSI identification recorded 2026-08-10: BSI-EL5-CEM00, HW D5, SW 4.04, PSA P/N 9819851480-01. The serial number is intentionally not embedded in this shared DBC.";
CM_ "CVM-family UDS DTCs B1004 and B117F are intentionally absent: diagnostic service responses are not periodic sensor signals and cannot be represented safely as fixed DBC fields. The exact CVM2/CVM3 generation is not proven by the current scan.";
CM_ "ABS/ESP identification recorded 2026-08-11 on 0x6AD->0x68D: Bosch ESP 9.0 / PyPSADiag ESP90, PSA references 9826694380 and 9812786180. UDS zones 2100..2103 were read in read-only mode; no CAN transmission or ESP write is authorized by this DBC.";

CM_ BO_ 520 "Validated engine speed, pedal position and torque. CruiseStateCandidate was correlated across several vehicle tests: raw 0 inactive, 2 active, 3 transient.";
CM_ SG_ 520 EngineRPM "Validated against idle setpoint and vehicle captures.";
CM_ SG_ 520 EngineTorqueNm "Validated by correlation with accelerator position while the engine was running.";
CM_ SG_ 520 AcceleratorPositionPct "Validated against the independent 0x228 accelerator channel.";
CM_ SG_ 520 CruiseStateCandidate "Vehicle-observed state. Active is derived as raw value 2; it is not an official PSA enum.";

CM_ BO_ 552 "Independent redundant accelerator channel used to validate 0x208. CHECKSUM/COUNTER were validated over 942978 local DLC-8 frames: CHK_INI=0x3, zero mismatches.";
CM_ BO_ 744 "Undocumented redundant accelerator copy; exact raw/2 formula confirmed against the validated accelerator signal.";
CM_ BO_ 749 "Function remains unidentified. Its protection is vehicle-validated over 239935 local frames: checksum in byte 0 high nibble, rolling counter in byte 0 low nibble, CHK_INI=0x2, zero mismatches.";
CM_ BO_ 757 "Steering torque frame protection was validated over 933226 local frames: checksum in byte 0 high nibble, rolling counter in byte 0 low nibble, CHK_INI=0xB, zero mismatches.";
CM_ SG_ 757 DriverTorqueRaw "Direction and dynamics validated on the vehicle. No physical Nm scale has been established, therefore the unit remains raw.";
CM_ SG_ 773 SteeringAngleDeg "Scale and direction validated on the vehicle.";
CM_ SG_ 773 SteeringRateMagnitudeDegS "Validated rate magnitude. Signed steering rate must be derived using SteeringRateSign: sign 1 means negative in the local replay.";
CM_ BO_ 781 "All four wheel speeds validated together over a road capture; mean inter-wheel spread 0.86 km/h.";
CM_ BO_ 809 "EAT6 status frame. CHECKSUM/COUNTER were validated over 476787 local frames: CHK_INI=0xD, zero mismatches. GearboxFaultCandidate is source-confirmed but no fault transition was available.";
CM_ SG_ 840 CurrentGear "Vehicle-validated mapping shared with the OBD replay: 0=N/no forward ratio, 1..6=engaged forward ratio (Drive), 9=Reverse. ReverseGearActive in 0x412 remains the redundant reverse source.";
CM_ BO_ 841 "EAT6 target/synchronisation frame. CHECKSUM/COUNTER were validated over 952844 local frames: checksum in byte 6 high nibble, counter in byte 6 low nibble, CHK_INI=0x6, zero mismatches.";
CM_ SG_ 841 TargetGear "Target gear uses the same observed 0, 1..6 and 9 coding as CurrentGear.";
CM_ SG_ 840 ESPAcknowledgedCandidate "Engine-to-ESP acknowledgement layout from the community AEE2010 definition. It was constantly 1 over 469307 local frames, so activation semantics are source-confirmed but not transition-tested.";
CM_ SG_ 840 ESPFaultStateCandidate "Engine-side two-bit ESP error state. It remained 0 over 469307 local frames; no fault transition was available for vehicle validation.";
CM_ BO_ 845 "ESP90 dynamics/intervention frame observed in 53 local learn sessions (477639 frames). The frame and rolling counter are present, but the active intervention bits remained zero; fields carrying Candidate in their names must not be treated as vehicle-validated activations.";
CM_ SG_ 845 ESPInterventionStateRaw "Observed state was 0 for 477637 frames and 6 for two adjacent frames. The enum meaning is unknown, therefore the raw state is exposed without an active/inactive inference.";
CM_ SG_ 845 ESPStatusInvalidCandidate "Source field P088_CutOffForbidden_OR_ESP_STATUS_INV. It was 1 for 39 frames in one short session; the two competing source meanings have not been resolved.";
CM_ SG_ 845 ESPInterventionActiveCandidate "Source field P147_Com_bESPIntvActv. It remained 0 in all 477639 local frames; layout known, active state not vehicle-tested.";
CM_ SG_ 845 TCSInterventionActiveCandidate "Source field P352_StbIntv_bTCSIntvActv. It remained 0 in all 477639 local frames; active state not vehicle-tested.";
CM_ SG_ 845 ESPExclusiveInterventionActiveCandidate "Source field P353_StbIntv_bESPExclvIntvActv. It remained 0 in all 477639 local frames; active state not vehicle-tested.";
CM_ SG_ 909 VehicleSpeedKph "Validated against the mean of the four wheel speeds; observed mean difference 0.35 km/h.";
CM_ SG_ 909 LongitudinalAccelerationMs2 "Validated by comparison with the derivative of vehicle speed.";
CM_ SG_ 909 CHECKSUM "PSA nibble-sum checksum with CHK_INI=0x7. Revalidated over 240282 local 0x38D frames with zero mismatches.";
CM_ SG_ 909 COUNTER "Four-bit rolling counter, layout cross-checked against the checksum-valid local captures.";
CM_ BO_ 941 "ESP EasyMove frame. ParkingBrakeState and frame protection are source-confirmed and locally observed. CHECKSUM/COUNTER: 480554 frames, CHK_INI=0xD, zero mismatches.";
CM_ SG_ 941 ParkingBrakeState "Observed counts over the checksum-valid corpus: state 0=405148, 1=74389, 2=496, 3=521. Source semantics confirm 0 released, 1 applied and 3 actuator moving; state 2 remains reserved/transition.";
CM_ BO_ 952 "Undocumented frame with two exact redundant engine/pedal formulas and one manually confirmed temperature candidate.";
CM_ SG_ 952 InteriorTemperatureCandidateC "Manually confirmed on the T9. The physical sensor location is not independently documented, so Candidate remains in the name.";
CM_ BO_ 969 "EAT6 protected frame. The local T9 uses DLC 8. CHECKSUM/COUNTER were checked over 952253 frames with CHK_INI=0xE; 952251 passed and two isolated frames were corrupt/outliers.";
CM_ SG_ 973 LateralAccelerationMs2 "Scale and direction validated during a road capture.";
CM_ SG_ 973 YawRateDegS "Scale and direction validated against steering and wheel-speed differential.";
CM_ SG_ 973 BrakePressureRelativeRaw "Validated as a relative brake-pressure indicator only. It must not be displayed as bar.";
CM_ BO_ 973 "Brake dynamics protection was checked over 961914 local frames with CHK_INI=0x3; 961913 passed and one isolated frame was a corrupt/outlier.";
CM_ BO_ 1010 "BSI to EPS lane-assist command. Observed locally at 20 Hz: 191254 frames across 53 sessions. In learn-20260805T081220Z-a182e602, the signed 11-bit torque field was nonzero for 536 frames in 10 coherent 20 Hz bursts at 66.07..84.99 km/h. Across the complete corpus, the angle, torque factor, lane-departure and LXA-mode fields stayed zero; the R3 reference fields DRIVE, counter, checksum and unknown4 also stayed zero. This is strong passive evidence for the older AEE2010 R2/EVO torque API, but the DBC remains receive-only and does not authorize transmission.";
CM_ SG_ 1010 LKAUnknownByte2Raw "Undocumented byte 2. It was 0x12 throughout every locally observed nonzero-torque frame; other inactive/fault states use different values. The experimental cristianku psa-torque branch currently emits 0x18 instead, so its frame template must not be copied to this vehicle without a dedicated state-machine validation.";
CM_ SG_ 1010 LKATorqueCommandRaw "Signed 11-bit BSI-to-EPS command layout cross-checked against cristianku/openpilot psa-torque at openpilot revision 18623d4c2044bf14c3e22cb6b6d6430e8950529f and opendbc revision 7884de3852cb03321be6f96a41d23e88eb85c835. Locally observed nonzero range -7..60 raw; 536 nonzero frames at 20 Hz while driving 66.07..84.99 km/h. Reading the same negative samples as unsigned would yield implausible discontinuities at 2041..2046. No physical Nm scale is asserted.";
CM_ SG_ 1010 LKAState "State table recovered from the PSA community definition and cross-checked against opendbc. Nonzero torque was observed with states Selected and Authorized; STATUS=4 Active was not observed, and STATUS=5 Defect was observed in other sessions.";
CM_ SG_ 1010 LaneDeparture "The source layout is known, but the field stayed zero in all 191254 local frames. Direction and activation semantics are therefore not vehicle-validated.";
CM_ SG_ 1010 LXAMode "Function selector, not an activation flag: 0=LKA, 1=LPA.";
CM_ SG_ 1010 LKATorqueFactorRaw "The current DBC represents this as 0..127 raw. It stayed zero in all 191254 local frames, including the ten nonzero-torque bursts. A historical community file used a 0.01 factor; neither its activation role nor its physical scale is asserted here.";
CM_ SG_ 1010 ColumnAngleSetpointDeg "Angle-command layout is source-confirmed. It remained zero in all 191254 local frames, including all ten nonzero-torque bursts, which strongly supports use of the torque rather than angle API on this T9.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 DriverDoorOpen "Source-confirmed at Dat_BSI.DRIVER_DOOR (byte 6 mask 0x08). Both closed and open states were observed locally; five learn sessions contain transitions.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 ParkingBrakeActive "Source-confirmed at Dat_BSI.PARKING_BRAKE (byte 0 mask 0x08). The active state was not observed in the 170566 local 0x412 frames inspected, so vehicle activation semantics remain untested.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 RearLeftDoorOpen "Undocumented byte 6 mask 0x20, confirmed by repeated closed-open-closed tests on the rear-left door.";
CM_ SG_ 1042 RearRightDoorOpen "Undocumented byte 6 mask 0x40, confirmed by repeated closed-open-closed tests on the rear-right door.";
CM_ BO_ 1069 "Protected BSI status frame. CHECKSUM/COUNTER were validated over 192087 local frames with CHK_INI=0xC, zero mismatches.";
CM_ BO_ 1106 "BSI driver/ACC command frame. Observed locally at about 20 Hz but with longitudinal regulation and ACC requests inactive; signal layout is source-confirmed for AEE2010 R3.";
CM_ SG_ 1106 SpeedSetpointChecksum "Two-bit parity code from the PSA source definition: bit 1 is the parity of the speed-setpoint high nibble and bit 0 the parity of its low nibble. Local 0x452 setpoints remained zero, so dynamic values are not vehicle-validated.";
CM_ SG_ 1106 FrameChecksum "Source field only on this non-ACC T9: the field and frame counter remained zero and the R3 CHK_INI=0x4 formula did not validate the local inactive payload. It must not be treated as a validated T9 frame checksum.";
CM_ BO_ 1294 "CruiseMode and CruiseActivationRequest were recovered from the original PSA source DBC and confirmed by local selector/road tests. Last-byte high nibble observed: 0x0 off, 0x2 cruise selected, 0x4 limiter selected, 0xA cruise active; the low nibble contains the rolling counter.";
CM_ SG_ 1294 XVVChecksum "Two-bit source-defined XVV/setpoint checksum. Values 0..3 were all observed and correlate with the selected RVV setpoint, but its generation algorithm is not yet proven; it is intentionally not named CHECKSUM to avoid generic PSA frame validation.";
CM_ SG_ 1294 BSIFrameCounter "Four-bit shared BSI frame counter. Consecutive 0x50E messages normally advance by two and locally carry odd values because this 10 Hz frame samples every second BSI counter state.";
CM_ BO_ 1293 "ABS state frame observed in 51 local learn sessions (95515 frames). The actual T9 DLC is 8, not 7 as in the comparison R3 DBC. Protection was revalidated over 96106 frames: CHK_INI=0xC, zero mismatches. ABSInterventionActiveCandidate remained 0 throughout.";
CM_ SG_ 1294 CruiseSetpointKph "Confirmed over five cruise engagements in four independent tests. Raw 255 means inactive/unavailable.";
